<title>UK: Royal Bank sets Singapore project finance.</title>
<headline>Royal Bank sets Singapore project finance.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Bank of Scotland Plc said on Tuesday it will set up a new Asia and Pacific region project finance group located in Singapore. Royal Bank said it has appointed Stephen Williams to the head the group and Jerry Chum as his deputy. Williams joins Royal Bank from Britain's biggest electricity generator National Power where he headed project finance for East Asia and Australasia and has previously worked for Midland Bank. Chum was previously with ANZ and Pacific Bank Berhad.</p>
<p>The new group will report to global project finance head Tom Hardy who is based in London.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
